Step 5/7: notes (numbers and years read from the data, never typed)

. *---------------------------------------------------------------------------
. local jy : word 1 of $R9_JUMP_YRS

. local nd : word count $R9_DOUBT_YRS

. local d1 : word 1 of $R9_DOUBT_YRS

. local d2 : word `nd' of $R9_DOUBT_YRS

. local fic ""

. * how much the set-aside records weigh: read from the yearly table in memory
. quietly summarize set_aside_share_firmyears_pct

. local fymax = ceil(r(max))

. quietly summarize set_aside_share_co2_pct

. local comax = round(r(max))

. if `fict_links' local fic "; firm links here are fictional, so those splits are only a pipeline check"

. local ntext "Notes: Each line treats all firms as one: total CO2 (or energy) over total value added (masked money unit
> s). Energy = gigajoules (GJ) of fuel and bought electricity (not all fuels); CO2 = energy times standard factors. Valu
> e added = output value minus materials, energy and services bought, at current prices, so price rises alone push the l
> ines down. Main line sets aside a firm-year whose energy per unit of value added is over $R9_RULE times that of its se
> ctor's middle (median) firm that year: at most `fymax' in 100 of a year's firm-years, yet up to `comax'% of a year's C
> O2; the line moves with this cut-off (companion table). Hollow gray: `jy' energy recording jump; `d1'–`d2' records par
> tly in doubt. Brackets: periods split up in R9-02 to R9-07 (firms getting cleaner, value added shifting, firms appeari
> ng or disappearing)`fic'. Shows totals only, not which firms changed or why."

. local notelines ""

. local line ""

. foreach w of local ntext {
  2.     if ustrlen("`line' `w'") > 138 & "`line'" != "" {
  3.         local notelines `"`notelines' "`line'""'
  4.         local line "`w'"
  5.     }
  6.     else local line = strtrim("`line' `w'")
  7. }

. local notelines `"`notelines' "`line'""'

. local nlines : word count `notelines'

. display "   notes: `nlines' lines"
   notes: 7 lines

. if `nlines' > 7 display as error "   WARNING: the notes run to `nlines' lines (limit 7)"

